Using differentiation rules, find the derivative of the following function:

{eq}f(y) = \displaystyle \log_7 \left ( \sin (\pi x) \right )

{/eq}

**

Assistant: **

To find the derivative of the given function, we apply logarithmic differentiation. We refer to the following differentiation rules:

1. Power Rule: {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[\log_a(x)] = \frac{1}{x \ln a}

{/eq}
2. Chain Rule: {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[u^n] = nu^{n-1} \frac{du}{dx}

{/eq}
3. Sum Rule: {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[f(x) \pm g(x)] = \frac{d}{dx}[f(x)] \pm \frac{d}{dx}[g(x)]

{/eq}
4. Derivative of Cosine and Sine: {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[\cos x] = -\sin x

{/eq} and {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[\sin x] = \cos x

{/eq}
5. Constant Rule: {eq}\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}[k] = 0

{/eq}

Applying these rules, we proceed as follows:

{eq}\begin{align}

\displaystyle f(y) &= \log_7 \left( \sin (\pi x) \right)\\[0.3cm]

&= \frac{\ln (\sin (\pi x))}{\ln(7)}\\[0.3cm]

&= \frac{\ln (\sin (\pi x))}{\ln(7)} + C \\[0.3cm]

f'(y) &= \frac{d}{dx} \frac{\ln (\sin (\pi x))}{\ln(7)} + C\\[0.3cm]

&= \frac{1}{\ln(7)} \frac{d}{dx} \ln (\sin (\pi x))\\[0.3cm]

&= \frac{1}{\ln(7)} \left( \frac{1}{\sin (\pi x)} \frac{d}{dx} \sin \pi x \right)\\[0.3cm]

&= \frac{1}{\ln(7)} \left( \frac{1}{\sin (\pi x)} \cos \pi x \cdot \pi \right)\\[0.3cm]

&= \mathbf{ \frac{\pi}{\ln(7)} \cot \pi x}

\end{align}

{/eq}

Therefore, the derivative of the given function is {eq}\displaystyle \mathbf{f'(y) = \frac{\pi}{\ln(7)} \cot \pi x}

{/eq}.

